# CONN — client to reflector.
#
# Source: M17 Protocol Specification, "M17 Internet Protocol (IP) Networking",
# section "Control Packets", Table 28 "Bytes of a CONN packet".
# Published at m17-protocol-specification.readthedocs.io/en/latest/ip_encapsulation.html;
# read from the archived copy at
# web.archive.org/web/20251008220102/https://m17-protocol-specification.readthedocs.io/en/latest/ip_encapsulation.html
# Address encoding: M17 spec Part I v2.0.4, Appendix A (spec.m17project.org/files/M17_spec.pdf).
#
#   bytes 0-3   43 4F 4E 4E   Magic, ASCII "CONN" (Table 28)
#   bytes 4-9   00 00 00 9F DD 51
#                             6-byte 'From' callsign, base-40, big endian
#                             (Part I §A.2). "AB1CD" is the spec's own worked
#                             example: 0x9FDD51.
#   byte  10    41            Module to connect to — single ASCII byte A-Z
#                             (Table 28). 0x41 = 'A'.
#
# Total 11 bytes.
434F4E4E 0000009FDD51 41
